content.text:
This paper presents YOLO-RoadSurvey, a practical method and prototype for Bandung municipal deployment. The main contributions are: 
• A trimmed YOLOv5s detection model pruned and quantized to 8-bit, achieving 95.4% vehicle/object detection accuracy on a Bandung-specific dataset at 12.3 ms end-to-end latency on an NVIDIA Jetson Xavier NX; 
• A lightweight U-Net with depthwise separable layers for pavement crack segmentation, reaching mean IoU = 0.83 and F1-score = 0.947 after targeted augmentation for wet-surface and low-light cases; 
• An integrated hardware-software architecture using STM32F407 for sensor IO, NVIDIA Jetson for inference, and Modbus TCP for telemetry; the field prototype was validated across 50 runs on two arterial corridors in Bandung producing continuous mapping and alerting outputs for maintenance scheduling. The measured power draw averaged 3.2 W at 12 V.
